    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302-a13">

                <pb facs="0499" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg429"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Señor Diaz to Mr. Otterbourg</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexican Republic, Headquarters of the East
                                Section of Government,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tacubaya,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-06-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 10, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Consul</hi>: I have received your note of the 5th
                    instant, in which you are pleased to ask of me a safe-conduct for Mr. Dano, in
                    order that in company of his secretary he may pass through the lines of the
                    forces besieging the capital; and in reply I comply with the duty of telling you
                    that, not being able to yield to your request without an express order, I shall
                    remit a copy of your note to the government of the nation for the proper
                    determination upon its contents.</p>
                <p>I protest to you the assurances of my personal consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>PORFIRIO DIAZ.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Consul</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of the United States in the City of Mexico.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
